+ * up) and T at `[x, 1, 1]` (front north, output south), each with its power port on the lane cell and `powerSide` the
+ * side from that cell into it. The units fill A, B, T in each column in `placeUnits`' order (`lowestFeedFirst`); a unit
+ * fed at another tier starts a new column with one empty column between, so two tiers' lanes never touch. The first
+ * column is `firstX` on the head's own feed tier, `firstX + 1` on any other. The logistics lanes `[x, 1, 0]` and
+ * `[x, 1, 2]` join at the tail through `[tailX, 1, 0..2]`; `spineZ` is 1 and the box is `[tailX + 1, 2, 3]`.
